                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is a turnover certificate for current account?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>CA-certified document confirming total business turnover for one or more FYs. Based on ITR, GST returns, or books. UDIN verified. Banks require it for current account KYC - especially for sole proprietorships without GST. Serves as accepted alternative to GSTIN for sub-threshold businesses. Prepared on CA letterhead with mandatory UDIN.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can I open a current account without GST registration?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. If turnover is below Rs 20 lakh (services) or Rs 40 lakh (goods), GST registration is not mandatory. Most Pune banks accept CA turnover certificate with sub-threshold declaration as alternative to GSTIN. Saves ongoing GST compliance cost. If a specific branch insists, try another branch of the same bank.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which banks in Pune accept the CA turnover certificate?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Most major banks: SBI, HDFC, ICICI, Kotak, Axis, Bank of Baroda, PNB, Bank of Maharashtra. Acceptance may vary by branch. We prepare in the format most commonly accepted by Pune branches and customise per specific requirements. If a branch is hesitant, we can speak with the branch manager.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What if my business is new and I have no ITR?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>For new businesses without ITR, the CA can certify turnover based on bank statements showing business credits, sales invoices, and projected turnover based on current run rate. Certificate notes ITR pending for first year. Most Pune banks accept this for new business current accounts with other KYC documents (Udyam, Shop Act, professional licence).</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much does it cost in Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Proprietor: Rs 1,000-2,000. Partnership/LLP: Rs 1,500-2,500. Company: Rs 2,000-3,000. Tender/GEM: Rs 1,500-3,000. Urgent same-day adds Rs 500-1,000. Payment after draft approval. No advance. One-time cost - no recurring fees unlike GST registration compliance.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is a turnover certificate the same as net worth certificate?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. Turnover certificate certifies total revenue/sales (how much the business earned). Net worth certificate shows assets minus liabilities (how much the business is worth). For current account opening, turnover certificate is typically sufficient. For bank loans, both may be needed. For visa, net worth is required. Our CA can prepare both simultaneously.</p></div>
